*** Services***
				-pods ip can be change so service helps and provide fixed address
*** Services types in k8***
	Cluster IP: used to communicate with internal cluster pods to pods communicate
	Node port: external(limited) it opens a port to a node (used for testing purpose)
	Load balancer:This sends a external traffic to pods use in production
		It sends traffic automatically to correct pods	
			it works on Application and Transport layer
	ExternalName: Maps a service to DNS name
	Headless service: In this cluster ip is not assigned and DNS goes directly to pods

**Deployments**
 A Deployment in Kubernetes manages a group of Pods and controls their lifecycle
 
 A Deployment provides:
	o Scaling (increase or decrease number of Pods)
	o Rolling updates (update Pods without downtime)
	o Rollback (revert to a previous version if needed)
	
ReplicaSets:
o A ReplicaSet ensures that a specified number of pod replicas are running at
any given time.

Affinity: It helps control where pods are scheduled based on rules
	types of affinity
		Node affinity: On which node pod will be assigned
		Pod affinity : Keeping pods in same no

Helm is k8s package manager
	Chart = collection of Kubernetes YAML files
	
Helm can manage:
	Deployment
	Service
	Ingress
	ConfigMap
	Secrets

Benefits of Helm:
	Reduces manual YAML work
	Easy installation
	Reusable templates
	Faster deployments
	Supports CI/CD
	Easy upgrades and rollback


